# Sudoku Design System Rules

This document defines how we keep UI consistent across iOS/Android/Web for Sudoku v1.

## Sources of truth

- Product requirements: `docs/sudoku-prd-v1.md`
- Screens/menus inventory: `docs/sudoku-screens-and-menus-v1.md`
- Settings inventory: `docs/sudoku-settings-v1.md`
- UI/UX (Figma Make): `https://www.figma.com/make/BXuIw8tGSZMaJcMeF439WT/Dark-Themed-Sudoku-UI-UX?t=Cn2IvBm76IroVvni-1`

### Policy: missing design elements in Figma

- If a required v1 feature/screen exists in PRD/docs but is missing in Figma, **flag the gap** and treat it as a product/design decision.
- Do not invent UI/UX beyond PRD/docs without explicit approval; keep any stopgap UI minimal and clearly temporary.

## 1) Tokens

### Location

- Put design tokens in a small TypeScript module (recommended path): `src/theme/tokens.ts`.
- Tokens should cover:
  - colors (including highlight and conflict states)
  - typography scale
  - spacing/radius

### Rules

- Prefer semantic tokens (e.g., `colors.grid.selectedBg`) over raw hex usage.
- Avoid ad-hoc “one-off” colors in components; add/rename tokens instead.

## 2) Styling approach (NativeWind)

- Prefer NativeWind `className` for layout and spacing.
- Prefer tokens for values that should remain consistent across the app (colors/typography/radii).
- If a platform-specific styling workaround is needed, isolate it behind a small helper instead of scattering conditionals.

## 3) Components

- Shared primitives should live in `src/components/**` (or `components/**`) and stay UI-only.
- Domain logic (Sudoku rules, eligibility, autosave) must not live in components (see `architecture.mdc` and `services.mdc`).

## 4) Accessibility (required)

- Keyboard support on web is a first-class requirement for the Sudoku grid.
- Never rely on color alone to convey state (selection, conflicts, same-number highlighting).
- All interactive elements must have accessible labels.

## 5) Deviations

When a UI deviation is required (platform limitation, performance constraint), document it briefly in the component (comment) and keep the token/component API consistent.
